-- title:
--   Compatibility of the level-ℓ formal family with π_ℓ
-- statement:
--   The data fall into the following groups.
--
--   **Numerical and arithmetic data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ and a nonzero natural number $N$ with $\bar r\neq r$ (`hrr`), $r\nmid N$ (`hrN`), $\bar r\nmid N$ (`hrbarN`) and $N$ squarefree (`hN`). A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), with $\mathcal O$ $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`) and $(r)=(\pi)$ (`hunr`); a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. A characteristic-zero domain $O^{nr}$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $O^{nr}$ is complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $O^{nr}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{nr}$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\bmod \pi$ (`hFr`). A monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet}\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) with `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **The indefinite side and its moduli.** Rationals $a,b$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite ($0<a$ or $0<b$) and is a division algebra at exactly the places containing $r$ or $\bar r$ (`hB`), and a maximal order $\Lambda$. A scheme $\mathcal X$ with $f\colon\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and a point assignment `pt` forming a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Gamma_0(N)$-level (`h𝒳`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on geometric points of algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). A level $n$ with $3\le n$ (`hn`), $r\nmid n$ (`hrn`), $\bar r\nmid n$ (`hrbarn`), $\gcd(n,N)=1$ (`hnN`); a fine moduli space $M\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point assignment `ptF` (`hM`), a group $G$ with $\rho\colon G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ and labels $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$ acting by twisting full level structures (`hρ`, whose seven clauses cover that $\rho$ is over the base, the twisting rule for `ptF`, and the multiplicativity, surjectivity and injectivity of $\chi$ modulo $n$). A forgetful morphism $p\colon M\to\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ (`hp`), invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`) and compatible with the point assignments (`hp_pt`). For every prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point assignment `ptT`, coarse moduli for curves with an extra level-$\ell$ structure (`h𝒴`), together with degeneracy maps $d_0,d_1\colon\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) realising forgetting the extra level (`hd₀`) and passing to the target of a level-$\ell$ isogeny (`hd₁`); Atkin–Lehner morphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}\colon\mathcal X\to\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ (`harf`, `harbarf`) implementing the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The definite side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`), a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (`hR₁`) contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hRΛ₁`), an idele $n_1$ in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r` (`hn₁`) such that `meetOrder R₁ n₁` is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`), an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0\colon\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`), and a height-one prime $v$ containing $r$ (`hv`). A subgroup $\Gamma^t$ of the unit group which is the group `awayUnits R₁ v` (`hΓt`); families $s_\ell$ of units and $sf_\ell$ of ideles whose four conditions (`hs`) say that $sf_\ell$ has component $s_\ell\otimes 1$ at every prime not containing $r$, component $1$ at the primes containing $r$, that the diagonal image of the scalar $\ell$ times $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and that $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$; the groups $\Gamma^t_\ell=\Gamma^t\cap s_\ell\Gamma^t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`); and a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma^t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **The special fibre.** The hypothesis `hΛℤ` that all integers lie in $\Lambda$, and a coordinate map $\mathrm{coord}\colon\Lambda\to W(\mathbb F_{r^2})^2$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord` (`hcoord`: additive, unital, multiplicative in the Frobenius-twisted sense, injective, dense, and compatible with reduced traces). A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $O^{nr}/(\pi)$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ on $A_0$, endomorphisms $e_\gamma,e'_\gamma$ of $A_0$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma^t$ with $e_\gamma$ over the base (`he`), degrees $\deg\gamma$, and `hA₀` asserting that $A_0$ is a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$. The hypotheses on these endomorphisms, summarised here, are: `hE1` ($e_\gamma,e'_\gamma$ an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the $\Gamma_0(N)$-level), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity up to powers of $r$), `hE1sc` (rational scalars act as multiplications up to powers of $r$), `hE1'` (the converse characterisation of scalars), `hE2` (for every injective ring homomorphism from the centraliser of the action of $X_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ realising each $e_\gamma$ by an endomorphism of the formal group whose matrix is $r^{k_\gamma}g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), `hE3` (for each full level-$n$ structure a labelling $\mathrm{lab}\colon\Gamma^t\to\Lambda$ describing the action of $e_\gamma$ on it, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$), and `hE4` (every $r$-power isogeny pair on a fake elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $e_\gamma$ up to powers of $r$). Further, an order $R_2\le R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) with $r$-power denominators over $R_1$ (`hR₂r`) and endomorphisms $\hat e$ of $A_0$ over the base (`hê`) satisfying `hE5a` (additivity, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action, preservation of level), `hE5b1`, `hE5b2`, `hE5b3` (unitality, multiplicativity, integers act as multiplications), `hE5c` (conjugate composes to the reduced norm), `hE5d` (compatibility with the $e_\gamma$ up to powers of $r$), `hE5e` (a joint matrix realisation of $\Gamma^t$ and $R_2$), `hE5g` ($R_2$ stable under the main involution); and the twin maximal order $\Lambda_1^{s}$ (`hΛ₁s`) containing $R_1$ (`hR₁Λ₁s`) with $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_1^{s}=R_1$ (`htwin`), an order $R_2'\le\Lambda_1^{s}$ (`hR₂'`, `hR₂'o`) with $r$-power denominators (`hR₂'r`) containing $R_2$ (`hR₂R₂'`), and endomorphisms $\hat e'$ (`hê'`) satisfying `hE6a`–`hE6c` (additivity and commutation, unitality, multiplicativity, integers, reduced norm), `hE6d` (extension of $\hat e$), `hE6e1`, `hE6e2` (stability under the involution, injectivity) and `hE6f` (if $\hat e'(z)$ annihilates the $q$-torsion for a prime $q\neq r$ then $r^{K}z\in q\Lambda_1^{s}$ for some $K$).
--
--   **The formal moduli package.** A ring homomorphism $\iota\colon W(\mathbb F_{r^2})\to O^{nr}$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $O^{nr}/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $O^{nr}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`); a family $\eta$ attaching to rigidified objects points of $MD$, with `hη` (three clauses: over Noetherian bases two admissible rigidifications have the same image exactly when they are isomorphic; compatibility with base change; local surjectivity along a Zariski cover); an injective ring homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the action of $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ in the precise sense of `hE₀`. A comparison $eD$ between the functor of points `ModuliPackage.G 𝒪 MD` and the product of the functor $B\mapsto\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal O}(O^{nr},B)$ with the functor $\Omega$ of Deligne data, subject to `hnatD` (naturality), `hbijD` (bijectivity), `hfstD` (the first component is the structural map $\psi$), `hGLD` (the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action corresponds to the $\mathrm{vdet}$-twisted action on Deligne data), `hPiD` ($\pi$-translation corresponds to one Frobenius twist of the first component) and `hPiexD` (existence of $\pi$-translates). A homomorphism $\kappa$ of residue rings with `hκ`, a natural number $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny from $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X_0$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner and isogeny data on $A_0$.** A curve $A_{0w}$ with morphisms $a_w,a_w',b_w,b_w'$ and exponent $k_w$ over the base (`haw`, `haw'`, `hbw`, `habw`) forming an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ (`hBSw`) preserving level (`hBSwlev`), together with the joint matrix realisation `hJOINTw` of $\Gamma^t$ and of $a_w\!\circ\! b_w$ as $\iota_0(\bar w)$ up to powers of $r$. Likewise, for each $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$: an extra level-$\ell$ structure $C_0(\ell)$ on $A_0$, curves $A_{0s}(\ell)$ with morphisms $a_s,a_s',b_s,b_s'$ and exponents $k_s$ (`has`, `has'`, `hbs`, `habs`), forming a level-$\ell$ isogeny (`hLIs`), an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_s}$ (`hBSs`) preserving level (`hBSslev`), with joint realisation `hJOINTs` involving $\iota_0(\mathrm{star}(s_\ell))$; and `hSTAB`, which says that $e_\gamma$ preserves $C_0(\ell)$ precisely when $\gamma\in\Gamma^t_\ell$.
--
--   **The uniformisation maps.** A family $\Xi$ sending rigidified curves over $\pi$-nilpotent Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras to points of `ModuliPackage.GPoint`, with `hΞleg` (over connected bases its $\psi$-leg is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality under base change of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves, up to powers of $r$) and `hΞdef` (the explicit description through $\eta$ and rigidified transport of $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0$). An element $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ together with the three equivariance hypotheses `heqΓ`, `heqW`, `heqS`, which say respectively that translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$, passing to the Atkin–Lehner $\bar r$-quotient, and passing along a level-$\ell$ isogeny correspond, under $\Xi$, to the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$, of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$ and of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\ell s^{-1})g_0^{-1}$ for some $c\in\mathbb Z$; the hypothesis `heqS` itself takes as input data $n_1$, $\ell$, $s$, $sf$ and the corresponding level-$\ell$ and basic isogeny data on $A_0$ with their joint realisation, summarised here.
--
--   **The formal family over $M$.** A group homomorphism $\theta_t\colon\Gamma^t\to G$ and a family $\Theta_f$ which, for every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, sends a triple $((\psi,P),g)$ — with $\psi\colon O^{nr}\to B$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$ and $g\in G$ — to a section $\operatorname{Spec}B\to M$ over $\mathcal O$, subject to `hnat` (naturality in $B$), `hG` (translating $g$ by $h$ and then applying $\rho(h)$ returns the original value), `hi'` (invariance under the $\mathrm{vdet}$-twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$, $\gamma\in\Gamma^t$, accompanied by left translation by $\theta_t(\gamma)$), `het` (unique lifting along surjections whose kernel has square zero in the stated pairwise sense) and `hfib` (over an algebraically closed field, two values agree exactly when they differ by some $\gamma\in\Gamma^t$ in the three stated ways: translation of $g$ by $\theta_t(\gamma)$, pullback of the Deligne datum along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, and agreement of $\psi'$ with the $(-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0\gamma))$-th Frobenius twist of $\psi$ on the elements fixed by the Frobenius powers coming from scalar elements of $\ker\theta_t$). Attached to $\Theta_f$ are the further hypotheses, summarised here: `hC0e` and `hC0u` (existence over connected bases, and uniqueness, of the norm-level transport of $P_0$ along a rigidification), `hC1e`, `hC1u`, `hC1p` (existence, uniqueness up to isomorphism, and base change of a rigidified curve whose $\Xi$-image has $\psi$-leg the twisted $\psi$ and whose Deligne datum is carried to $(\psi,P)$ by the twisted action of $g_0^{-1}$), `hC2` (for such data, the value of $\Theta_f$ at $g=1$ is the section `ptF` of the pair consisting of the curve and the transported level structure), `hC2c` (that section followed by $p$ is the section `pt` of the curve), `hC3` (the effect of the $\Gamma^t$-action: the transported level structures differ by the twist labelled $\chi(\theta_t(\gamma))$, and extra level structures compatible with a given one on $A_0$ determine the same subscheme), `hC4` (the same for the action of an arbitrary unit $h$ and an integer power of $r$), `hC4pi` (the effect of $\pi$-translation), and `hC5` (the criterion, over algebraically closed fields, for two such rigidified curves to be isomorphic, with the accompanying identification of level and extra level structures). Finally `hCLe` and `hCLu` give existence and uniqueness of an extra level-$\ell$ structure on $E$ compatible with a prescribed one on $A_0$ for primes $\ell\neq r$ invertible in $B$, and the families $\Theta_T(\ell)$ into the nilpotent points of $\mathcal Y_\ell$ are natural (`hnatT`) and take the value `ptT` at compatible data (`hVT`).
--
--   **The level-$\ell$ data.** A prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$; a scheme $M_\ell\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point assignment `ptFℓ` which is a fine moduli space for fake elliptic curves with a full level-$n$ structure and an extra level-$\ell$ structure (`hMℓ`); a morphism $\pi_\ell\colon M_\ell\to M$ over $\mathcal O$ (`hπℓf`) compatible with the point assignments (`hπℓ`); a morphism $p_\ell\colon M_\ell\to\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\mathcal O$ (`hpℓg`) compatible with the point assignments (`hpℓ`); an action $\rho_\ell\colon G\to\operatorname{Aut}M_\ell$ over the base (`hρℓf`), intertwining $\rho$ through $\pi_\ell$ (`hρℓπ`), leaving $p_\ell$ invariant (`hρℓp`) and implementing the $\chi(h)$-twist on pairs of full and extra level structures (`hρℓtw`). Lastly a family $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ which, for every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, sends $((\psi,P),g)$ to a section $\operatorname{Spec}B\to M_\ell$ over $\mathcal O$, and which is natural in $B$ (`hnatℓ`), satisfies the same $\rho_\ell$-equivariance as $\Theta_f$ (`hGℓ`), and has the prescribed value at $g=1$ (`hvalℓ`): whenever $\varrho$ is a rigidification of a curve $E$ over $B$ relative to $A_0$ and the $(-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0))$-th Frobenius twist of $\psi$, the $\psi$-leg of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ equals that twist, the Deligne datum attached by $eD$ to $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ is carried to $(\psi,P)$ by the twisted action of $g_0^{-1}$, $P_n$ is the norm-level transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho$, and the extra level structure $C$ on $E$ is compatible with $C_0(\ell)$ in the stated sense, then $\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi,P),1)$ is the section `ptFℓ` attached to $(E,P_n)$ and $C$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every Noetherian commutative ring $B$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with the image of $\pi$ nilpotent, and for every $x=((\psi,P),g)$ in the value at $B$ of the product functor $\big(\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal O}(O^{nr},-)\times\Omega_{K_0,\pi}\big)\times \underline{G}$, the section $\Theta_{f,\ell}(x)$ of $M_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}B$, followed by $\pi_\ell$, equals $\Theta_f(x)$ as a section of $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}B$; that is, post-composition with $\pi_\ell$ carries $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ to $\Theta_f$ on all Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent bases.
--
--   In the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the quaternionic Shimura curve, this is the rigidity statement that a natural, $G$-equivariant formal family into the level-$(n,\ell)$ fine moduli space with the prescribed value at $g=1$ necessarily lifts the corresponding family on the level-$n$ space through the forgetful morphism $\pi_\ell$. It is used in the construction of compatible formal families along the Hecke tower away from $r$ and $\bar r$.
